<p>This thing is the shadow of another world's sun &#8212; a star from some other reality whose light and image are leaking into our own.</p>
<p>Sunlight is a defining force, metaphorically speaking (and in metaphysics and magic, metaphors have power). Light makes vision possible; shadows define the edges of things. Solar cycles give us our seasons, dictate many of our activities, shape our very perception of time. The spectrum of a star defines the niches in which photoautotrophs might evolve to make a living under it; those autotrophs, in turn, define the shapes of biospheres.</p>
<p>Standing in the light of <em>another</em> sun&#8230; well, that has the power to <em>re</em>define.</p>
